---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import djSideProfile from '../assets/images/mobius-nyc-gala-dj-side-profile.jpeg';
import djMixerCloseup from '../assets/images/mobius-nyc-gala-dj-mixer-closeup.jpeg';
import djGuestsBooth from '../assets/images/mobius-nyc-gala-dj-guests-booth.jpeg';
import rooftopPractice from '../assets/images/rooftop-dj-practice-nyc-skyline.jpeg';
import williamsburgRooftop from '../assets/images/williamsburg-rooftop-dj-set-night.jpg';
import lisbonCafe from '../assets/images/lisbon-pasteis-de-nata-cafe.jpeg';
import lisbonCooking from '../assets/images/lisbon-cooking-class-pasteis-de-nata.jpeg';
import mammoth from '../assets/images/mammoth-snowboard-trip-summit-group.jpeg';
import rooftopParty from '../assets/images/nyc-rooftop-party-announcement-july-2026.jpeg';

const artists = [
  'The Marías', 'Sara Bareilles', 'Not For Radio', 'Creedence Clearwater Revival',
  'The Doobie Brothers', 'Silver', 'Boston', 'Gloria Gaynor', 'berlioz', 'Ambrosia',
  'Nirvana', 'Selena', 'Steely Dan', 'The Smiths', 'Jimi Hendrix', 'The Internet',
  'Jungle', 'Faye Webster', 'Daft Punk', 'TV Girl', 'Men I Trust', 'Jamiroquai', 'Sade',
  'feeble little horse', 'Khruangbin', 'The Police', 'PinkPantheress', 'Wallows',
  'Clairo', 'Jordan Ward', 'Nia Archives', 'Daniel Caesar', 'Anderson .Paak',
  'Kali Uchis', 'Joji', 'Travis Scott', 'Dominic Fike', 'Surf Curse',
  'The Neighbourhood', 'Eagles', 'Red Hot Chili Peppers', 'Baby Keem', 'A$AP Rocky',
  'Frank Ocean', 'Phoebe Bridgers', 'SZA', 'Tyler, The Creator', 'Bad Bunny',
  'Cage The Elephant', 'Gorillaz', 'Playboi Carti', 'Kanye West', 'Kendrick Lamar',
  'The Weeknd',
];
---

<section id="life">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="section-label">Life &amp; Hobbies</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">The other half of the story</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Robots pay the bills, but this is the rest of it: DJ sets, discography deep-dives,
      trips, and whatever's cooking.
    </p>

    <div class="feature-row">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <h3>DJing</h3>
        <p>
          Karl got into DJing because his fraternity brothers at MIT (Theta Tau) were already
          into it. He picked it up socially, and it has grown into a real hobby since. He
          describes himself as an "amateur," but what he values about it is how portable and
          spontaneous it is: he mixes casually in his apartment, shows up to Prospect Park in
          Brooklyn to DJ just because, or sets up at a friend's event on an hour's notice. Most
          of what he plays, he finds digging through SoundCloud.
        </p>
        <ul class="gear-list">
          <li><strong>Software</strong> djay Pro (Algoriddim)</li>
          <li><strong>Controller</strong> Pioneer DDJ-FLX4</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          It traces back further than the fraternity, too. Karl took MIT's "DJ History,
          Technique, and Technology" course and appeared in an MIT student DJ showcase video
          before it became a standing hobby: apartment sessions, the Williamsburg rooftop set
          below, and a full DJ booth at the Möbius Industries NYC open house gala.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-photos">
        <figure class="tall">
          <Image src={djSideProfile} alt="Side profile of Karl DJing at the Mobius Industries gala, purple event lighting" width={800} height={1000} />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image src={djMixerCloseup} alt="Close-up of Karl's hands on a DJ mixer at the Mobius Industries gala" width={800} height={600} />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="photo-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <figure class="span-6">
        <Image src={djGuestsBooth} alt="Karl DJing at the Mobius Industries gala with guests chatting nearby" width={900} height={650} />
        <figcaption>Möbius Industries NYC open house gala, June 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-3">
        <Image src={rooftopPractice} alt="Karl practicing DJing solo on a rooftop with the Manhattan skyline behind him" width={450} height={650} />
        <figcaption>Solo rooftop practice, NYC</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-3">
        <Image src={williamsburgRooftop} alt="Karl DJing at a nighttime rooftop gathering in Williamsburg, Brooklyn" width={450} height={650} />
        <figcaption>Williamsburg rooftop set</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <h3>54 discographies and counting</h3>
        <p>
          Separately from DJing, Karl has kept a running habit since 2023: pick an artist, and
          listen to their entire discography start to finish, in chronological order. It is a
          screenshot-tracked list, 54 artists so far and likely an undercount of his real total,
          spanning classic rock, soul and funk, grunge, Tejano, bedroom pop, hip-hop, R&amp;B,
          and reggaeton. Below is the actual list, in no particular order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="artist-cloud-wrap">
        <p class="artist-cloud-label">Full-discography deep dives, chronologically, since 2023</p>
        <ul class="artist-cloud">
          {artists.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row reverse" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <h3>Travel</h3>
        <p>
          A solo surf trip to Portugal, Lisbon and Ericeira, in June 2026, which turned into as
          much of a food trip as a surf trip, including a hands-on Portuguese pastry class
          making pastéis de nata. A snowboard trip to Mammoth, CA in March 2026 with friends,
          granite peaks and all. A snowboard trip to Chile in August 2026. Somewhere in there,
          Ultra Music Festival in Miami, two years running.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-photos">
        <figure class="tall">
          <Image src={lisbonCooking} alt="Karl in a Home Cooking Lisbon apron, pouring custard into pastry shells during a pasteis de nata cooking class" width={800} height={1000} />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image src={lisbonCafe} alt="Karl holding a plate of two pasteis de nata in a Lisbon cafe" width={800} height={600} />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="photo-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <figure class="span-12">
        <Image src={mammoth} alt="Three men at a snowy Mammoth, CA mountain summit with snowboards, granite peaks in the background" width={1600} height={700} />
        <figcaption>Mammoth, CA, March 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row" style="margin-top: 4rem;">
      <div class="feature-text">
        <h3>Cooking, hosting, and everything else</h3>
        <p>
          Beyond the trips and the turntables: cooking, arts and crafts, raves and live music,
          and a lot of time spent with friends. In July 2026 he threw a rooftop party in New
          York and gave an impromptu announcement to the crowd, the kind of thing that happens
          when you are the one who planned it.
        </p>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="chip">Cooking</span>
          <span class="chip">Hosting</span>
          <span class="chip">Raves &amp; live music</span>
          <span class="chip">Arts &amp; crafts</span>
          <span class="chip">Time with friends</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-photos">
        <figure class="span-12" style="grid-column: span 2;">
          <Image src={rooftopParty} alt="Karl giving an announcement into a microphone at a rooftop party he hosted, crowd cheering around him, NYC skyline at dusk" width={1000} height={750} />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
